    "description": "EFC bridge table mapping (K0, m^2) -> (mu, Sigma) as a function of (k, a). R(k,a) = K0 * Theta(rho_m(a)) * (Gamma_prime * phi_dot)^2 * a^4 / k^4; mu = 1/(1+R); eta = 1 + ((eta_ref - 1)/R_ref)*R capped at 2; Sigma = 0.5*(1+eta)*mu. At (a=1, k=0.05 h/Mpc) this reproduces (mu, Sigma) = (0.94, 1.05) exactly.",
    "notes": [
      "Row a = 1 is the present day.",
      "At k = 0.05 h/Mpc (CMB lensing scale) and a = 1, (mu, Sigma) = (0.94, 1.05) reproduces the MGCAMB + cobaya sweet spot with Planck plik_lite TTTEEE + lowl + lensing.clik, giving \u0394chi\u00b2 = -0.45 vs GR (Localization paper Phase 2).",
      "GR is recovered at galactic / solar-system densities via Theta(rho) -> 0 and at small-scale high-k via R -> 0.",
      "This table is a reference bridge between the two EFC field parameters (K0, m^2) and the MGCAMB mu0-Sigma0 sampling variables used in efc_bridge.yaml."
    ]
  },
